        "0x6ece400",
        "0x6ece484",
        "0x6ece4c0",
        "0xc5eaf8",
        "0x1c0620"
      ],
      "conclusion": "AudioWaveformView keeps pendingSamples, displayedSamples and offset in LazyState. frameRate is Double1/30. Timeline uses AnimationTimelineSchedule whose paused argument is !sampling. Both observed onChange registrations use initial=false. Date changes drive offset updates and samples-reference changes append novel Float samples. AnimationTimelineSchedule.minimumInterval is nil (x0=0, optional tag1) and the static guard byte84d40ec is0.",
      "limits": [
        "frameRate caps the integration step. It is not an observed device-frame-rate measurement. Runtime behavior of the schedule wrapper selected by flag84d40ec is unverified."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "V533-W03",
      "validation": "verified_static",
      "evidence_type": "official_artifact_observation",
      "offsets": [
        "0x6fc955c",
        "0x6fc95b4",
        "0x6fc969c",
        "0x6fc96d4",
        "0x6fc973c",
        "0x6fc974c",
        "0x6fc99c8"
      ],
      "conclusion": "On each Date change, elapsed=newDate.timeIntervalSince(oldDate). If the low bit of flag84d40ec is set, callback returns. Otherwise dt=min(frameRate,max(elapsed,0)), offset+=dt*velocity. When offset>lineWidth+spacing, exactly one column is processed and offset decreases by that pitch. Equality does not process a column. There is no catch-up while loop in this function.",
      "limits": [
        "Nonfinite values and caller invalid geometry are outside this finite-input reconstruction. Global flag semantics remain unknown."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "V533-W04",
      "validation": "verified_static",
      "evidence_type": "official_artifact_observation",
      "offsets": [
        "0x6fc95e8",
        "0x6ece580",
        "0x6ecea30"
      ],
      "conclusion": "Incoming collection snapshots are compared by longest overlap. Starting with min(old.count,new.count) and decreasing to1, compare old.suffix(k) with new.prefix(k) using per-Float ==. Append only new.dropFirst(k) for the first matching overlap. With no overlap, append all new values. Empty novel suffix leaves pending state unchanged.",
      "limits": [
        "Float comparison uses fccmp, so NaN does not match itself. This overlap algorithm also treats identical repeated snapshots as no new data."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "V533-W05",
      "validation": "verified_static",
      "evidence_type": "official_artifact_observation",
      "offsets": [
        "0x6fc97dc",
        "0x763b130",
        "0x763b218",
        "0x765be14",
        "0x6fc9890",
        "0x6fc99a0"
      ],
      "conclusion": "When a column boundary is crossed and pendingSamples is nonempty, compute arithmetic sum starting from additive zero, divide by count, and append that Float mean to displayedSamples. Pending samples are cleared after the boundary processing. The current drawn history is retained in this bounded function.",
      "limits": [
        "No displayed-history pruning is present in the inspected update function. An independently bounded storage policy would be an implementation adaptation."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "V533-W06",
      "validation": "verified_static",
      "evidence_type": "official_artifact_observation",
      "offsets": [
        "0x6fc980c",
        "0x20ce68",
        "0x6fc986c",
        "0x763b2bc",
        "0x763b4dc",
        "0x763b528",
        "0x763b834",
        "0x763b878"
      ],
      "conclusion": "With no pending samples, take displayedSamples.suffix(5) and call763b2bc. For count<2, return first, including nil for empty. Larger collections compute mean and regression-like arithmetic over collection.indices. Zero denominator returns last. A nonnil result is appended, nil adds nothing.",
      "limits": [
        "The generic loop uses collection.indices, and the suffix retains its original indices. Do not silently rebase its indices to0 or substitute last-value/zero/noise. Complete Float-exact fallback formula is retained as a bounded unresolved branch below."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "V533-W07",
      "validation": "verified_static",
      "evidence_type": "official_artifact_observation",
      "offsets": [
        "0x6ece734",
        "0x6ece780",
        "0x6ece7b8",
        "0x6ece884",
        "0x6ece8d0",
        "0x6ece968"
      ],
      "conclusion": "Drawing uses pitch=lineWidth+spacing and columnCount=floor(width/pitch)+1. Iterate newest displayed sample first from the right. Column i has x=width-i*pitch-offset. Present lineHeight=max(minHeight,min((height-lineWidth)*Double(normalizeSample(sample)),height-lineWidth)). Missing samples use the same clamp with value0 and missingSampleColor. For lineHeight>0, stroke a vertical centered segment using supplied StrokeStyle. For zero height, fill an ellipse centered at(x,height/2) with diameter lineWidth.",
      "limits": [
        "Offsets are function-level anchors plus precise raw assembly. No random waveform, fixed number of bars, interpolation between neighboring bars or peak/RMS computation appears in this drawing leaf."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "V533-W08",
      "validation": "verified_static",
